#Дизайн_Derived_Graph_Viewer<[
Базис:
  Пользователь не должен строить Work Graph вручную; граф является наблюдаемой проекцией задач, evidence, memory, target files, provider runs and domain artifacts.
  Operator dashboard уже задаёт роль человека как оператора/reviewer, а operator-dashboard.snapshot.v1 задаёт derived read model без browser-side raw .bvc parsing.
  Language Adapter Layer and OneBase artifact mapping уже дают будущие structured file/domain facts for graph nodes and edges.
Вектор:
  Derived graph viewer renders relationships from workgraph.snapshot.v1 plus optional operator-dashboard.snapshot.v1, Evidence v1, MemoryRecord v1, Worker Output/provider run summaries and language/domain adapter projections.
  Graph is read-only by default: no manual node creation, no manual edge drawing, no layout-as-state and no React Flow-like editor as the main product path.
  MVP starts from WorkItem dependencies, target files, legacy evidence strings and dashboard snapshot summaries; later graph slices add structured evidence, memory, provider runs and OneBase domain objects when their producers materialize them.
Цель:
  Оператор получает понятную карту проекта and can focus a task, inspect why it is connected, and open task/file/artifact details without turning graph editing into a second source of truth.

Проверки:
  graph viewer не поддерживает ручное создание нод как основной режим
  описаны derived nodes/edges for work, files/artifacts, evidence, memory, provider runs and OneBase objects
  выбран renderer/layout recommendation with MVP/later boundary
  integration uses dashboard snapshot and Work Graph as source of truth

Метки:
  atom.profile: plan
  design.id: derived-graph-viewer
  design.input: workgraph.snapshot.v1, operator-dashboard.snapshot.v1, evidence-record-v1, memory-record-v1, worker-output-v1, adapter-projection-v1
  design.output: derived-graph-view.v1
  work.source: design-derived-graph-viewer
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Purpose_And_Non_Goals<[
Базис:
  The graph exists to explain relationships already present in project state, not to author project state.
Вектор:
  Purpose: show task dependency chains, current/ready/blocked focus, evidence links, target file/artifact impact, memory context and domain object relationships around selected WorkItems.
  Purpose: help the operator answer "why is this task ready/blocked?", "what files and domain objects does it touch?", "what evidence proves it?", and "what memory/context will the worker see?".
  Non-goal: manual graph editor, freeform node canvas, drag-to-create dependencies, visual layout as canonical state or React Flow-like manual editing overhead.
  Non-goal: replacing backlog board, task detail drawer, atom inspector form, language adapters, memory store or evidence model.
  Non-goal: graph database as source of truth in MVP; graph data is rebuildable from Work Graph and derived projections.
Цель:
  Keep the graph as an explanatory projection that complements dashboard/detail views without competing with Work Graph runtime.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: derived-graph-viewer-purpose-nongoals
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Derived_Node_Model<[
Базис:
  Node types must map to existing contracts so the viewer can be rebuilt and tested from snapshots.
Вектор:
  WorkItem node: id, title, status, ownerRole, department, priority, risk, traceStatus, nextAction and checks from workgraph.snapshot.v1 items.
  Artifact/File node: path, kind, language/domain adapter id, confidence and source range when available; MVP starts with targetFiles and protocol/artifact refs from evidence strings.
  Evidence node: Evidence Record v1 id/type/status/source/summary/artifacts/command/provider/runId; MVP can show legacy evidence summaries as compact evidence nodes.
  MemoryRecord node: MemoryRecord v1 id/type/status/confidence/summary/sourceWorkItem/evidenceIds/relatedFiles/relatedTasks.
  ProviderRun node: Worker Output or run summary with provider, runId, taskId, status, started/finished time when available, failureReason/retryAdvice and produced evidence ids.
  OneBase domain object node: document, catalog, register, report, widget, posting script, procedure or runtime artifact from adapter/domain projections; use onebase.kind, onebase.name, trace.source.file and confidence.
Цель:
  The viewer can mix operational tasks with code/domain context while preserving each node's source contract and confidence.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: derived-graph-node-model-v1
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Derived_Edge_Model<[
Базис:
  Edges should explain existing relations and never imply a writeable graph model.
Вектор:
  depends_on: WorkItem dependency edges from workgraph.snapshot.v1.edges or item.dependsOn, directed dependency -> dependent task.
  targets: WorkItem -> Artifact/File from item.targetFiles and structured evidence artifacts.
  has_evidence: WorkItem -> Evidence from legacy item.evidence or structured Evidence v1 records with taskId.
  produced_by_run: Evidence -> ProviderRun and ProviderRun -> WorkItem from Worker Output/provider run summaries.
  creates_or_updates_memory: WorkItem/Evidence -> MemoryRecord from sourceWorkItem, evidenceIds, relatedTasks and relatedFiles.
  relates_file: MemoryRecord/Evidence/ProviderRun -> Artifact/File from relatedFiles, artifacts and changedFiles.
  domain_relation: OneBase document -> posting script -> registers -> report/widget readers from adapter projections and domains/onebase/artifact-mapping.bvc.
  trace_ref: WorkItem/Evidence/MemoryRecord -> domain object or source range when adapters expose trace refs with confidence.
Цель:
  Edge labels remain small, typed and rebuildable, allowing filters and focus views without hand-authored graph state.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: derived-graph-edge-model-v1
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Renderer_And_Layout_Decision<[
Базис:
  The first implementation should be useful inside the current small Node/HTML UI without pulling in a visual editor framework.
Вектор:
  Recommendation for MVP: implement a simple read-only SVG/HTML graph panel first, generated from a derived graph JSON, with dependency/file/evidence lanes or grouped columns and no external graph editor dependency.
  Recommendation for interactive later stage: Cytoscape.js with Dagre or ELK layout for focus/expand/collapse, larger node counts, keyboard navigation and stable layout presets.
  Keep Mermaid or Graphviz as optional export/debug renderers for static diagrams, not as the main interactive viewer, because operator interactions need focus, filters and click-through details.
  Avoid React Flow as the primary approach because its strengths are manual canvas editing and custom node workflows, which are explicit non-goals for this viewer.
  Layout strategy: default to layered left-to-right or top-to-bottom dependency flow; cluster by WorkItem status, domain, artifact kind or selected focus; collapse evidence/memory leaves by default.
Цель:
  Start with the smallest read-only renderer that fits the existing UI server, while preserving a clear upgrade path to Cytoscape.js + Dagre/ELK when interaction complexity justifies it.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: derived-graph-renderer-layout
  renderer.mvp: svg-html-readonly
  renderer.later: cytoscape-dagre-elk
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Interaction_Model<[
Базис:
  Graph interaction should deepen inspection and navigation, not mutate canonical project state.
Вектор:
  Filter by node kind, WorkItem status, department, ownerRole, priority, risk, evidence status, memory type, provider, artifact kind and domain.
  Focus on a WorkItem, artifact, evidence record, memory record, provider run or OneBase object; focus view shows one-hop neighbors first and can expand upstream dependencies, downstream dependents, files, evidence, memory and domain links.
  Expand/collapse groups: collapse evidence leaves, memory leaves, file folders, OneBase artifact groups, done tasks and low-confidence adapter results by default.
  Open task detail: selecting a WorkItem opens the existing dashboard/backlog detail drawer with BVC, labels, checks, evidence, target files and run/memory summaries.
  Open file/artifact: selecting a file/domain artifact opens file path or artifact detail when the host can open resources; otherwise copy/show stable path and trace ref.
  Explain edge: selecting an edge shows source contract, confidence and the field that produced it, such as dependsOn, targetFiles, evidence.artifacts, memory.relatedFiles or onebase.register.refs.
Цель:
  The operator can move from high-level graph context into concrete task/file/evidence detail while keeping all state changes behind existing runtime actions.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: derived-graph-interactions
  trace.status: verified
]>

#MVP_Vs_Later<[
Базис:
  The design task should not implement a renderer beyond a tiny future path; it should define a bounded first graph scope.
Вектор:
  MVP includes a derived graph projection function/schema and read-only view around WorkItem nodes, depends_on edges, target file nodes, legacy evidence nodes and click-through to the existing task detail drawer.
  MVP uses current /api/snapshot or operator-dashboard.snapshot.v1 as input and can be served by the existing Node UI server as an additional route or tab.
  MVP excludes graph editing, persistence of visual layout, custom drag/drop authoring, provider transcript replay, full graph DB, full OneBase parser implementation and broad renderer dependencies.
  Later adds structured Evidence v1 nodes, MemoryRecord nodes, ProviderRun nodes, OneBase domain object nodes, adapter confidence indicators, Cytoscape.js + Dagre/ELK, search/focus URL state and static Mermaid/Graphviz export.
  Later may materialize derived graph JSON as NDJSON/SQLite/GBC cache only when size or latency requires it; source of truth remains Work Graph plus structured evidence/memory/artifact projections.
Цель:
  First ship a small explanatory graph, then enrich it as structured producers become available.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: derived-graph-mvp-later
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Integration_With_Dashboard_And_WorkGraph<[
Базис:
  Dashboard snapshot already separates display-ready state from canonical Work Graph state.
Вектор:
  Work Graph .bvc remains canonical for WorkItems, statuses, dependencies, target files, evidence strings and trace status.
  workgraph.snapshot.v1 supplies base WorkItem nodes and depends_on/target file edges; operator-dashboard.snapshot.v1 supplies current/ready/blocked focus, recentEvidence, workerRunSummaries and memoryUpdates.
  Evidence v1, Project Memory v1 and adapter projections are optional inputs that enrich the derived graph without changing the Work Graph snapshot contract.
  UI integration path: add a Graph tab or "open graph focused on this task" affordance in operator dashboard/backlog detail; the graph consumes derived graph JSON and returns selected ids to the detail drawer/router.
  Runtime integration path: expose a buildDerivedGraphView(snapshot, projections) style function later, mirroring buildOperatorDashboardSnapshot and keeping graph projection deterministic and testable.
  Trace verification: graph edges should expose source fields and confidence so trace.status can be reviewed without guessing from rendered positions.
Цель:
  The derived graph viewer becomes another rebuildable read model beside the dashboard snapshot, not a separate task source or visual editor.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: derived-graph-dashboard-workgraph-integration
  trace.status: verified
]>
